N:until 1848,according to V.Sylvester and J.Richardson,and yet a couple
N:of
N:tunes ago we were apparently in 1834.Secondly,whoever pricked it down
N:wa
N:not at all familiar with the polka rhythm,especially the time
N:sig..Eithe
N:"T.Williams,1834" refers to something other than the collection date,or
N:John Clare put the MS down for a few years and came back to it in a fit
N:of sanity, or enthusiasm for the new dance rhythm, or somebody else
N:entirely was responsible for entering this tune(not by any means rare
N:in
N::fiddlers tune books)Reference to the original MS may c
